WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.150
- Hi, I'm Renee Zellweger,

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.977
and this is how I became
Judy for the movie "Judy."

00:00:03.977 --> 00:00:06.168
(horn music blaring)

00:00:06.168 --> 00:00:09.918
♪ Somewhere over the rainbow ♪

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.910
I started in the car with
Judy and my imagination,

00:00:16.942 --> 00:00:21.590
in the passenger seat, and
my laughter and embarrassment

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.940
at contorting my body and howling,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.520
trying to make these
sounds come out of my face

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.940
for the first time ever.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.020
Her music playing all the
time, or her interviews.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.710
I was always listening to her voice,

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.380
and anything I could get my
hands on, just to feel like

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.660
we were conjuring the essence of her.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.730
I loved watching her with Mickey Rooney

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.480
on her television show.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.000
You could see her charm.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.740
You could see what a sweet
friend she would've been.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.630
You see how smart she was.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.060
Funny, just so funny.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.300
And you have to be so
smart to be that funny.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.750
I loved watching her performances

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.460
on "The Judy Garland Show."

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.278
When she sang, especially "The
Battle Hymn of the Republic,"

00:01:03.278 --> 00:01:08.278
when her friend, President
Kennedy, was assassinated,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:12.300
she sang that song as a tribute to him.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.830
It's a gorgeous
representation of the power

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.620
of her ability to emote through her voice

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.893
in a way that will touch you,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.190
I mean for keeps, very special.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.758
- Your suite has been released.

00:01:27.758 --> 00:01:29.235
- What do you mean released?

00:01:29.235 --> 00:01:30.440
Where exactly has it gone? (chuckles)

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.780
The clothes were fitted
to an assumed posture,

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.610
so they didn't zip up in
the back unless I stood

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.120
like I was supposed to stand,
so it was really helpful

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.070
if I ever got lazy, the
dress would not let me forget

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.750
what I was supposed to be doing.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:50.030
Very helpful to be disciplined
by antique sequins,

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:54.130
so that was a pretty
big part of feeling like

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.780
you're just a little bit closer

00:01:58.246 --> 00:02:00.991
to a representation of the lady.

00:02:00.991 --> 00:02:05.991
♪ And the dreams that you dare to dream ♪

00:02:06.539 --> 00:02:09.451
♪ Really do come true. ♪

00:02:09.451 --> 00:02:12.060
It was this collaborative
series of experiments,

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.447
just trying things.

00:02:14.447 --> 00:02:17.537
It started with, "Come on
over, and we'll just try

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.927
"a couple of looks, and
we'll try some recordings

00:02:20.927 --> 00:02:23.990
"just to see where we are,
and where we might get to."

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.110
And then, we started
trying some dance moves,

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.990
and trying some clothes, and
we just kept trying things

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.130
until here we are. (laughs softly)

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.937
I think I remember the first time I heard

00:02:33.937 --> 00:02:36.210
"Come Rain or Come
Shine," I started laughing

00:02:39.134 --> 00:02:41.100
(laughs heartily) 'cause
I felt like somebody lied.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.040
They moved the goal posts.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.437
You know, they said, "Here, try and do

00:02:45.437 --> 00:02:48.820
"this vocal performance,"
where, you know, she really

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.990
was having difficulty
accessing her instrument.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:56.410
And then, they sent that
recording. (laughs heartily)

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:57.810
I'm still laughing.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.810
And then, working with Matt, thankfully,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:05.040
who was our extraordinarily
talented composer,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.160
and Jeff, who's a music producer,

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.590
and Andrew, who was playing
piano and doing warmups,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:14.520
and Paul, who were all
there for all of it,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.987
and just making it feel possible.

00:03:17.987 --> 00:03:19.227
"We'll do it again, let's do it again.

00:03:19.227 --> 00:03:20.877
"Okay, no one more
time, we'll do it again,

00:03:20.877 --> 00:03:21.710
"we'll do it again.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.597
"Okay, 10 more times, we'll do it again.

00:03:23.597 --> 00:03:24.950
"Okay, now you have to stop

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.330
'cause "you won't talk tomorrow, so stop."

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.820
And when it came time to
do the actual performances,

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.610
I felt like I had my stage
moms (laughs) off to the side

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.217
going, "Yes you can, it's gonna be fine,

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.070
"it's gonna be fine."

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.110
And I'm sure they were all
like, (sighs and laughs),

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.740
but anyway, in this moment,

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.100
I would love to say thanks to those guys

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.800
'cause it's not possible
without all of them,

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.760
and Rupert and David and everybody around.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.381
It was a team effort, for sure.

00:03:56.381 --> 00:03:57.706
You won't forget me, will you?

00:03:57.706 --> 00:04:00.123
(applauding)

00:04:00.972 --> 00:04:02.049
♪ In a moment ♪

00:04:02.049 --> 00:04:03.225
Promise you won't.

00:04:03.225 --> 00:04:04.058
(applauding and cheering)

00:04:04.058 --> 00:04:06.340
(warm orchestral chord)

